Emotional engagement fundamentally extends product lifespans by creating personal attachment, meaning, and identity connection between users and products. Products designed to be loved are more likely to be cared for, repaired, and kept longer, reducing replacement cycles and material consumption. This strategy leverages psychological research showing that emotional attachment predicts longevity behavior more strongly than rational appeals about environmental impact. Design for emotional engagement includes aesthetic excellence, storytelling, personalization, and opportunities for users to invest emotional labor in products.